stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    state "No artefact - collection refused" as None
    state "SPDI written consent on record" as Spdi
    state "Withdrawn - data path closed" as Withdrawn
    state "Both regimes on record, each tagged" as Both
    state "DPDP-regime record only, new enrolment" as Dpdp
    state "Imported evidence, original date kept" as Imported

    [*] --> None
    None --> Spdi: Written consent captured before collection, SPDI r.5 sub-rule 1
    None --> Imported: Migration attaches dated evidence the employer already holds
    Imported --> Spdi: Evidence accepted as the SPDI artefact
    Spdi --> Withdrawn: Employee withdraws in writing, SPDI r.5 sub-rule 7
    Withdrawn --> None: A new purpose needs a new artefact
    Spdi --> Both: Switch date reached, on or about 13 May 2027
    None --> Dpdp: First collection after the switch, capture rule set by counsel
    Dpdp --> Withdrawn: Withdrawal where consent is the basis
    Both --> Withdrawn: Withdrawal of the consent-based purpose

    note right of Both
        No artefact is rewritten, re-dated or discarded at the switch.
        Whether the SPDI Rules survive the omission of s.43A is CR-12.
        Written capture stays on by default until counsel answers.
    end note

    note right of None
        Payroll is never blocked by a missing artefact.
        Bank-detail capture waits for the artefact and pay goes by the
        tenant's configured non-bank disbursal mode, FR-CHR-102.
        Biometrics wait, and attendance uses the non-biometric path.
    end note
